<section class="section white"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">The Signature Finish Protocol</p><h2>No project closes without a formal quality gate.</h2><p>The Signature Finish Protocol happens after construction is complete and before the project officially closes.</p><ul class="check-list"><li>Detailed walkthrough of all completed work with the client</li><li>Photo documentation of every finished area</li><li>Punch-list review and resolution of remaining items</li><li>Client sign-off confirming the work meets the written scope</li></ul></div><img class="rounded-image" src="/assets/images/bathroom-detail.jpg" alt="Finished Mid City bathroom project"></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">What we stand on</p><h2>Standards that protect both sides.</h2></div><div class="value-grid"><article><h3>Documentation over memory</h3><p>Written scopes, photo-verified stages, and formal sign-offs. If it is not documented, it did not happen.</p></article><article><h3>Transparency over salesmanship</h3><p>You get the real scope, timeline, and cost. We do not lowball work and rely on preventable change orders later.</p></article><article><h3>Licensed trade compliance</h3><p>Work requiring licensed electrical, plumbing, or HVAC professionals is performed by verified New York trades.</p></article></div></div></section>
